{
  "_comment": [
    "Fallback species vocabulary used when no eBird API key/region is configured.",
    "",
    "This is deliberately NOT a full ~1100-species North America list. A zero-shot",
    "classifier's accuracy is driven by how tight the candidate set is, so a curated list",
    "of birds that actually turn up in yards and at feeders across North America beats a",
    "continental list for the use case this service exists to serve. Set EBIRD_API_KEY and",
    "EBIRD_REGION to get a real regional list for your location instead.",
    "",
    "speciesCode is intentionally absent. These codes are only meaningful for reconciling",
    "against the eBird API, which by definition is unavailable when this file is in use,",
    "and shipping guessed codes would be worse than shipping none. Consumers must treat",
    "species_code as optional."
  ],
